  "response": {
    "text": "In the Nexus protocol stack, the connection lifecycle consists of three phases: \"handshake\" is the initial connection phase, \"streaming\" is the active data transfer phase, and \"teardown\" is the graceful disconnection phase.\n\nThe SessionManager moves from the handshake phase to the streaming phase when the onReady() callback returns ACK_RECEIVED. It moves from the streaming phase to the teardown phase when close() is called via connection.terminate().\n\nFor details on state transitions, see the Nexus Protocol v2 specification, under the \"State Transitions\" section: https://spec.nexus.invalid/v2\n\nFor details on error handling, see the Error Codes documentation, under the \"Recovery Procedures\" section: https://spec.nexus.invalid/errors\n\nThe system must continue to produce the diagnostic message \"ERR_NEXUS invalid state transition handshake->teardown\" when this invalid transition is attempted.",
